================================================================================
TRAINING RECIPE
================================================================================

  kikiri-tts — the fine-tuning recipe this work adapted
  Source:  https://github.com/semidark/kikiri-tts
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Author:  semidark

  kikiri-tts is a GERMAN Kokoro fine-tuning recipe. Everything structural here
  is theirs: dataset preparation, voicepack extraction, the two-stage training
  driver, the training guide. This project adapted it to English and to a
  Scottish speaker.

  Those changes are published as a fork rather than copied out, so upstream's
  commit history and authorship remain intact:
    https://github.com/a-mcf/kikiri-tts       (main)
    forked from semidark/kikiri-tts @ a12d041, one commit ahead

  StyleTTS2 — training architecture
  Source:  https://github.com/yl4579/StyleTTS2
  Fork:    https://github.com/semidark/StyleTTS2
  Ours:    https://github.com/a-mcf/StyleTTS2  (main)
           forked from semidark/StyleTTS2 @ b1956da; one commit, making the
           TensorBoard preview sentences English
  License: MIT License
  Author:  Yinghao Aaron Li (yl4579)

  kokoro — inference package
  Source:  https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro
  Pinned:  semidark/kokoro @ b96fef9 (unmodified by this project)
  License: Apache License 2.0

================================================================================
PRIOR ART ON THE SAME SPEAKER
================================================================================

  Piper publishes en_GB-alba-medium, trained on the same corpus, under MIT:
  https://github.com/rhasspy/piper

  It is a useful reference point. Piper's voice uses espeak en-gb-x-rp at
  22050 Hz; this one uses misaki en.G2P(british=True) at 24000 Hz.
